{"type": "survey_submit", "survey_type": "post", "puzzle_idx": null, "answers": {"puzzle_1_rate_again": 2, "puzzle_1_guesses": "never", "puzzle_2_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_2_guesses": "never", "puzzle_3_rate_again": 3, "puzzle_3_guesses": "never", "puzzle_1_rating_reason": "A lot of \"free\" lines that add up to 10 (including spaces)\nA lot of the free lines were also at the edges so the information was very easy to use I guess?\nLots of big numbers I think", "puzzle_2_rating_reason": "Not a lot of easy lines at the start relatively?\nA lot of the first steps I did were in the middle as opposed to the edges which made things a bit harder to think about? \nA lot more smaller numbers", "puzzle_3_rating_reason": "A lot of smaller numbers and few free lines but everything started on the left, so it kind of felt like solving a 5x10 and then the other half was really easy since I already had so much info", "strategy": "find the lines that add up to 10 (including spaces)\nFiguring out which of the numbers the cells are a part of helped so I could cross out a lot of nearby squares\nFor big numbers, you can usually get the center squares for free", "comments": "In a lot of other nonograms, they usually form a picture so you kind of get a free hint as to what the general shape should look like but these ones were more random"}, "t": "2026-05-20T15:28:57.225259+00:00"}
{"type": "session_end", "t": "2026-05-20T15:21:50.477968+00:00"}
